{"name":"Blue Agave","hex":"#b1c6c7","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue agave","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any member of the species Agave tequilana of agave plants used in making tequila."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue_agave"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blue agave","blocks":[{"text":"Agave tequilana, commonly called blue agave or tequila agave, is an agave plant that is an important economic product of Jalisco state of Mexico, due to its role as the base ingredient of tequila. The high production of inulin in the core of the plant is the main characteristic that makes it suitable for the preparation of alcoholic beverages."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Agave_tequilana_1.jpg/330px-Agave_tequilana_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_agave","wikidata":"Q311065"},{"title":"Agave","blocks":[{"text":"Agave is a genus of monocots native to the arid regions of the Americas. The genus is primarily known for its succulent and xerophytic species that typically form large rosettes of strong, fleshy leaves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Agave_americana_R01.jpg/330px-Agave_americana_R01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agave","wikidata":"Q155874"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant 